## 5. Software Guide: Getting Started with #LancsBox X

### Installation & Corpora Management
1. Download `#LancsBox X` for free at **[lancsbox.lancs.ac.uk](https://lancsbox.lancs.ac.uk)** (auto-selects Windows, macOS, or Linux installers; manuals, videos, exercises, and helpdesk are on the same page)[cite: 16].
2. Add corpora via three methods[cite: 16]:
   * **Corpus Hub:** Download pre-built corpora such as **BNC 2014 v.2**[cite: 16, 17].
   * **Own Data:** Select local files, name the corpus, pick the language, and enable grammatical (POS) and semantic annotation[cite: 16].
   * **Web Scraping:** Enter corpus name, language, seed URLs, maximum websites to scrape, and external link depth, then click **Create corpus**[cite: 16].

### Multi-Tool Workspace
* Combine windows for **KWIC**, **Text**, **GraphColl**, and **Words**[cite: 16].
* Hold `Ctrl` + click to highlight multiple tool tabs and search across all active tools simultaneously[cite: 16].

### Search Syntax Cheat Sheet (Case-Insensitive by Default)[cite: 16]

```text
# 1. Simple Word & Phrase Searches
love                                              # Exact word form (case-insensitive)
new zealand                                       # Multi-word phrase
I love going                                      # Exact expression

# 2. Wildcard Searches
new*                                              # Matches 'new', 'newspaper', etc.

# 3. Smart Searches (Type in ALL CAPS)
PASSIVE                                           # Verb 'to be' + optional adverbials + past participle
TIME                                              # All words in the 'Time' semantic category
ADJECTIVE NOUN VERB                               # Grammatical POS sequence

# 4. Corpus Query Language (CQL) — Enclosed in Square Brackets []
[word="new"]                                      # Word attribute match
[word="new" & pos="J.*"]                          # 'new' tagged as an adjective (regex POS)
[sem="E2.*"]                                      # Words in semantic category E2 (Emotion)
[hw="sit" & pos="V.*"] [word="through"] within s  # All verb variants of lemma 'sit' (sit, sits, sat, sitting)
                                                  # followed by 'through' within a single sentence (s)
```
[cite: 12, 13, 16]

